p.src:
The most compact household rule in the lecture belongs here too. The hospital-administration speaker says a mentor told him to live on what he made five years ago and invest and bank the rest. In bookkeeping form, $\begin{aligned}
C_t &\approx Y_{t-5},\\
S_t &= Y_t-C_t,\end{aligned}$ so that $S_t \approx Y_t-Y_{t-5}.$ This is not a universal consumption model. It is a source-conscious discipline rule: if the lifestyle lags the income, the gap becomes deployable capital.

